## Task 2 - Create a Volume and upload files

1. Click **Catalog**, navigate to `{{ cat }}` → `default` schema, click the top right **Create** → **Volume**.

    {{ shot('04-genie-agent/4-5-01-create-volume.png', 'Create > Volume') }}

2. Enter `{{ s.naming.volume }}` for **Volume name**, select **Managed volume** for **Volume type**, then click **Create**.

    {{ shot('04-genie-agent/4-5-02-volume-form.png', 'Enter Volume details') }}

3. Click **Upload to this volume** in the top right of the created Volume screen and upload the {{ v.docs | length }} PDFs from Task 1.

    {{ shot('04-genie-agent/4-5-03-upload-files.png', 'Upload files') }}

4. Verify the {{ v.docs | length }} PDFs are now in the Volume.

    {{ shot('04-genie-agent/4-5-04-uploaded-files.png', 'Uploaded files') }}

## Task 3 - Connect the Volume to Genie Agent

1. Click **Configure** in the top right of the Genie Agent screen, then click **Add** on the **Sources** tab.

    {{ shot('04-genie-agent/4-5-05-add-source.png', 'Configure > Sources > Add') }}

2. Select **Volume** from the menu. Type `{{ s.naming.volume }}` in the search field, select `{{ s.naming.volume }}` from your catalog (`{{ cat }}.default`), then click **Confirm**.

    !!! info "If Volume doesn't appear in the menu"
        If the menu only shows **Table**, **Metric View**, **SQL function**, then **Analyze Files in Volumes with Genie Agents** Preview hasn't been enabled. Ask your workspace administrator to enable it. If you select a Volume and click **Confirm** but it doesn't appear in the Sources list, your workspace can't use Lakebase.

    {{ shot('04-genie-agent/4-5-06-select-volume.png', 'Select Volume') }}

3. The `{{ s.naming.volume }}` Volume appears in **Sources** with **Indexing…** status. Click the pencil icon to the right of `{{ s.naming.volume }}` to see **Content Search Status** showing **Indexing in progress**. Genie is indexing documents so it can read them, which takes a few minutes.

    {{ shot('04-genie-agent/4-5-06b-indexing.png', 'Indexing Volume') }}

    !!! warning "Wait for indexing to complete before asking questions"
        If you ask questions before indexing finishes, Genie might not find document content. Verify the status in the **Sources** list changes from **Indexing…** to **Indexed** before moving to Task 4.

    {{ shot('04-genie-agent/4-5-06c-indexed.png', 'Volume indexing complete') }}

4. Click the pencil icon next to **Description** on the same screen and enter the text below, then click **Save**. Genie uses this description to decide which questions should reference documents.

    ```text
    {{ v.description | trim | indent(4) }}
    ```

    {{ shot('04-genie-agent/4-5-07-volume-description.png', 'Enter Volume Description') }}

## Task 4 - Ask questions in Agent mode

!!! warning "Only Agent mode reads documents"
    In **Chat** mode, Genie doesn't read Volume documents and will say "{{ v.chat_mode_symptom }}." To analyze both documents and data together, you must ask in **Agent** mode.

1. Close the **Configure** panel, click the **New chat** icon in the top right, then verify **Agent** is selected in the mode toggle below the input box.

    {{ shot('04-genie-agent/4-5-08-agent-mode.png', 'Select Agent mode') }}

2. Enter the question below.

    !!! prompt "Prompt"
        ```text
        {{ v.questions[0].prompt }}
        ```

3. {{ v.questions[0].verify | trim | indent(4) }}

    {{ shot('04-genie-agent/4-5-09-doc-answer-1.png', v.questions[0].shot_alt) }}

4. In a new conversation, ask in Agent mode:

    !!! prompt "Prompt"
        ```text
        {{ v.questions[1].prompt }}
        ```

5. {{ v.questions[1].verify | trim | indent(4) }}

    {{ shot('04-genie-agent/4-5-10-doc-answer-2.png', v.questions[1].shot_alt) }}

